== the tab reads back the ledger it has been writing to ==
  ok — the tab can read its own ledger
  ok — through the shared forward layer rather than a second reader of its own
  ok — minRr is the spec's own T1 in R (0.1875), not the 2R a caller gets by omitting it — judging a 0.75 ATR target against a 2R bar would score it on a target it never had
  ok — an unrecorded mechanic reads null, never a guess
  ok — and a missing name is safe
  ok — the WATCH tag survives either way
  ok — with an empty ledger the card says exactly that
  ok — and that it accumulates without the reader doing anything
  ok — a firing records (P80W-15M-LONG)
  ok — and the tab can now read that mechanic back
  ok — under the name it was written with
  ok — still a WATCH
  ok — a recorded-but-unsettled firing still reads as nothing settled — fired and waiting is not measured
  ok — the card consults the ledger rather than asserting over it

== the forward panel is wired, and empty-safe ==
  ok — it renders a string even with nothing recorded
  ok — naming the ledger it reads
  ok — and nothing renders as NaN or undefined
  ok — wired into render
  ok — in the FULL branch, below the SIMPLE early return

== the census measures why the spec is silent ==
  ok — the census carries a coincidence measurement
  ok — long: each condition's own frequency is counted
  ok — long: as proportions of evaluable bars
  ok — long: and what independence would have predicted is their product
  ok — long: the pair can never be commoner than either half
  ok — long: rarerBy is the ratio between them (1.0x)
  ok — short: each condition's own frequency is counted
  ok — short: as proportions of evaluable bars
  ok — short: and what independence would have predicted is their product
  ok — short: the pair can never be commoner than either half
  ok — short: with the pair never occurring the ratio is null, not Infinity — a ratio against nothing is not a finding
  ok — no bars means no measurement rather than a zero
  ok — the census renders the measurement, and asks its question rather than announcing its answer — it said "Trend and pullback are not independent; they fight each other" above a table free to measure the opposite
  ok — with the independence prediction beside the observed pair, which is what makes the ratio mean anything
  ok — and states the mechanism in words, as the expectation being tested
  ok — a pair far below the independence prediction reads as rarer than chance
  ok — and one ABOVE it reads as commoner — the old prose could only ever say rarer
  ok — a pair landing on the prediction reads as independent, not as a conflict
  ok — and one that never co-occurs says so
  ok — trend at 100% is reported as a fact about the window rather than as independence
  ok — the side itself is NOT scored as a finding the bars cannot support
  ok — a trend that holds on every bar cannot measure an interaction
  ok — and neither can a pullback that does
  ok — a trend that holds on no bar cannot measure an interaction
  ok — and neither can a pullback that does
  ok — a trend that holds on every bar cannot measure an interaction
  ok — and neither can a pullback that does
  ok — a trend that holds on no bar cannot measure an interaction
  ok — and neither can a pullback that does
  ok — nothing claims the two conditions hold about half the time — a sentence the table on this very fixture contradicts
  ok — with every side degenerate the panel says the window cannot answer, not that it answered no
  ok — which would be a finding these bars did not produce
  ok — while a window that DID measure independence says so
  ok — and the bands either side of 1.0 are named as display thresholds, not significance
  ok — nothing renders as NaN or undefined
  ok — and it renders nothing at all rather than an empty table when there is no census
  ok — a pair that never co-occurs reads "never" rather than Infinity

== and it still refuses to invent a rate from what it resolved ==
  ok — no win rate is computed anywhere in the code
  ok — the resolved list says so in as many words
  ok — and says why
  ok — pointing at the thing that can answer it instead

== the tab publishes its verdict so the alert file never has to re-derive it ==
  ok — hg80AlertRows is exported
  ok — and so is the publisher
  ok — published setups match the takeable count at a venue that can pay
  ok — and at one that cannot — which is zero, so nothing is sent
  ok — the two fixtures really do differ, so that pair of assertions can fail
  ok — a published setup names the instrument and the rung it came from
  ok — and the side it fired on
  ok — carrying the plan the card would print, not a level invented downstream
  ok — and the candle it fired on, which is what the alert file keys on
  ok — with the breakeven priced off the PLAN, as hg-v799 settled — not the rung's last bar
  ok — hg80AlertRows does not consult the focus — a 5m row must not go unsent because somebody left the view on 1d
  ok — the publisher puts the rows on the window
  ok — and publishes an empty result rather than nothing, so "the tab looked" is distinguishable
